        "text": "50"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "100"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "11"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Two-digit form",
        "body": "Write a number up to 99 as $10t + u$ with digits $t$ and $u$. Its digit sum is $t + u$, and the difference is $10t + u - (t + u) = 9t$. So 1 to 99 give only the values $0, 9, 18, \\dots, 81$: 10 different numbers (one for each tens digit $t = 0, \\dots, 9$).\n\nThe number 100 gives $100 - 1 = 99$, a new value. In total there are 11 different results.\n\n**Answer: (E) 11**"
      }
    ],
