    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Point D belongs to the side AB of triangle ABC so that triangle ADC is equilateral and its area is half the area of triangle ABC. What is the measure of $\\angle CBA$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$20^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$25^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$27.5^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$30^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$45^\\circ$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "D is the midpoint",
        "body": "Triangles ADC and DBC have the same height from C onto line AB. Since ADC has half the area of ABC, it also has the same area as DBC, so $AD = DB$.\n\nADC is equilateral, so $DC = AD = DB$: triangle DBC is isosceles with apex D. Its angle at D is $180^\\circ - 60^\\circ = 120^\\circ$, so each base angle is $\\frac{180^\\circ - 120^\\circ}{2} = 30^\\circ$. Hence $\\angle CBA = 30^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $30^\\circ$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Circle through A, B, C",
        "body": "As above, D is the midpoint of AB and $DA = DB = DC$. So C lies on the circle with diameter AB and $\\angle ACB = 90^\\circ$. With $\\angle CAB = 60^\\circ$, the third angle is $\\angle CBA = 180^\\circ - 90^\\circ - 60^\\circ = 30^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $30^\\circ$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
