    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "List the possible positions",
        "body": "Number the rows 1–5 from the top and the columns 1–5 from the left. The grid has cells in row 1: columns 1–2; rows 2 and 3: columns 1–4; rows 4 and 5: columns 3–5. A $2 \\times 2$ shape fits in exactly 7 positions; let $x_1, \\dots, x_7$ be how often each is used:\n\n- $x_1$: rows 1–2, columns 1–2\n- $x_2$: rows 2–3, columns 1–2; $x_3$: rows 2–3, columns 2–3; $x_4$: rows 2–3, columns 3–4\n- $x_5$: rows 3–4, columns 3–4\n- $x_6$: rows 4–5, columns 3–4; $x_7$: rows 4–5, columns 4–5\n\nEach placement adds 4 to the total, so the sum of the grid is $4(x_1 + \\dots + x_7)$.\n\nThe visible numbers give: row 2, column 1 is covered only by positions 1 and 2: $x_1 + x_2 = 3$. Row 2, column 3 is covered only by positions 3 and 4: $x_3 + x_4 = 3$. Row 4, column 4 is covered by positions 5, 6 and 7: $x_5 + x_6 + x_7 = 4$.\n\nSo $x_1 + \\dots + x_7 = 3 + 3 + 4 = 10$, and the sum of all numbers is $4 \\cdot 10 = 40$. (The 5 in row 3, column 2 says $x_2 + x_3 = 5$, which is consistent.)\n\n**Answer: (B) 40**"
      }
    ],
